commit fd1b55747de31d843577fcee3cc9d9cd5915a86b
fix(T-01/T-02): maya stub scaffold + P0 correctness repairs
T-01: tests/maya_stub/ — semantic fakes for maya.cmds / maya.api.OpenMaya
with real DAG scene graph, row-major matrix math, and correct 8-corner
world-bbox transforms. Self-verified by test_maya_stub.py; mayapy tier
documented in docs/testing.md (manual-only, never CI).

T-02 P0 repairs (each pinned by a regression test):
- server.execute_code / _execute_scene_code: raise MayaExecutionError on
  CommandResponse.error instead of silently dropping Maya-side failures
- scene_tools: all generated code now JSON-serializes args via _scene_call
  (kills the rules_escaped / *_escaped interpolation injection surface)
- measure/conflicts/_predict_conflicts/_suggest_layout: shared _world_bbox
  helper transforms all 8 bbox corners (rotation/scale-safe)
- measure clearance: signed AABB separation (euclidean over separating
  axes, negative = penetration depth) — fixes min_clearance false-negatives
- all sampling caps (aesthetics 200, overlaps 80, conflicts 60, layout 100,
  pair windows) now disclose checked/skipped
- scene_assert: exists:false honored for missing objects; bbox_min added
- get_zone_map reports total_objects; zone coverage no longer always -4x
- create_orbit_camera creates LOC_<name>_target locator + real aim
  constraint instead of aiming at None
- server/types docstrings: drop hallucinated get_output(), point to the
  real maya://sessions/{key}/output resource

Verification: pytest 333 green (284 baseline + 49 new), ruff 245->184,
mypy 277->227, wheel builds, stdio init + tools/list(18) + ping probe OK

